1
00:00:01,292 --> 00:00:02,668
"Previously on The Mentalist..."

2
00:00:02,919 --> 00:00:04,212
Agent Lisbon, Tommy Volker.

3
00:00:04,337 --> 00:00:07,924
I've got somebody here who says Cassie
Flood was murdered by Tommy Volker.

4
00:00:08,049 --> 00:00:09,842
Show Volker this sketch
and watch his face.

5
00:00:10,134 --> 00:00:11,219
Do you recognize this man?

6
00:00:11,344 --> 00:00:13,429
Agent, I know you're under
a lot of pressure right now.

7
00:00:13,596 --> 00:00:15,932
So I don't want you to worry
that you've offended me in any way.

8
00:00:16,098 --> 00:00:17,141
You don't know what he's like.

9
00:00:17,266 --> 00:00:20,728
Amanda, I promise nothing
is gonna happen to you

10
00:00:20,853 --> 00:00:22,647
as long as you
do the right thing.

11
00:00:27,485 --> 00:00:30,988
She left a suicide note, you know...
laying blame at your feet.

12
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:35,243
You will not get away with this.
I promise.

13
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:42,333
What did you want
to see me about?

14
00:00:42,458 --> 00:00:45,253
A warrant for Thomas Volker's
personal and business records.

15
00:00:45,419 --> 00:00:48,297
- I've already ruled on that.
- But we've got fresh evidence.

16
00:00:48,965 --> 00:00:53,219
We believe that Thomas Volker was involved
in killing this reporter, Cassie Flood.

17
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:55,596
She was investigating
Volker Industries' involvement

18
00:00:55,721 --> 00:00:57,640
in the massacre
of a South American village.

19
00:00:57,765 --> 00:00:59,725
Right. I remember.

20
00:00:59,976 --> 00:01:03,145
I convinced his assistant,
Amanda Shaw

21
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:04,897
to testify against him,
and he killed her for it.

22
00:01:05,064 --> 00:01:08,693
- Made it look like a suicide.
- Okay, saying it does not make it so.

23
00:01:09,193 --> 00:01:11,696
Yes, but I ordered
a second autopsy

24
00:01:12,071 --> 00:01:15,157
by a forensic pathologist
who specializes in suicide.

25
00:01:16,033 --> 00:01:18,077
The ligature marks
on Amanda's neck

26
00:01:18,202 --> 00:01:20,580
are not consistent
with suicide by hanging.

27
00:01:21,247 --> 00:01:22,290
She was murdered.

28
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:26,419
You know, I'm surprised
that you got Gail Bertram

29
00:01:26,544 --> 00:01:29,046
to cough up for a second opinion
on a closed case.

30
00:01:29,797 --> 00:01:31,549
He didn't.
I paid for it myself.

31
00:01:34,302 --> 00:01:36,596
Agent Lisbon,
why are you doing this?

32
00:01:38,389 --> 00:01:40,391
He's a murderer.
If we follow the money

33
00:01:40,516 --> 00:01:42,643
we'll find who he paid
to kill these women.

34
00:01:43,603 --> 00:01:45,605
Why are you doing this?

35
00:01:47,315 --> 00:01:50,484
I looked Amanda Shaw in the eye
and I promised I'd protect her.

36
00:01:52,069 --> 00:01:53,112
I failed.

37
00:01:54,947 --> 00:01:58,743
I know that you've heard this before
but you are not responsible for her death.

38
00:01:59,869 --> 00:02:02,872
I respectfully disagree.
I need to make this right.

39
00:02:03,122 --> 00:02:05,416
This report gives us
plenty for a warrant.

40
00:02:07,335 --> 00:02:08,377
All right.

41
00:02:08,502 --> 00:02:12,256
You do realize that Volker Industries is one
of the biggest employers in the state

42
00:02:12,715 --> 00:02:15,051
and that Tommy Volker is a huge
supporter of the governor?

43
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:17,720
Yes, and that
they're also good friends.

44
00:02:18,888 --> 00:02:22,308
That's why I came to you because
I know that you won't be threatened

45
00:02:22,433 --> 00:02:24,226
by a man's status or connections.

46
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:30,191
Well, this...
report does change things.

47
00:02:32,693 --> 00:02:36,489
I'm inclined to open up the door
a crack but just a crack.

48
00:02:37,573 --> 00:02:39,492
Don't make me regret it,
Agent Lisbon.

49
00:02:55,257 --> 00:02:58,552
Lisbon, you're distracted
and you have an eager gleam in your eye.

50
00:02:59,887 --> 00:03:02,390
Either you have a breakthrough
in the Volker case

51
00:03:02,723 --> 00:03:04,392
or you're in love.
Which is it?

52
00:03:04,558 --> 00:03:06,477
I got Judge Davis
to sign the warrant

53
00:03:06,602 --> 00:03:09,397
and Van Pelt should be getting
Volker's records momentarily.

54
00:03:09,522 --> 00:03:11,107
I was hoping it was love.

55
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:13,984
You deserve happiness,
but I'm glad for you anyway.

56
00:03:15,403 --> 00:03:17,988
Jane Doe.
No wallet, phone, or I.D.

57
00:03:18,239 --> 00:03:20,282
Sanitation workers
found the body around 6:00 a.m.

58
00:03:21,534 --> 00:03:26,664
Designer clothes. Sample size.
She's as tall as a giraffe.

59
00:03:27,915 --> 00:03:29,750
- A model.
- Looks like a mugging gone wrong.

60
00:03:30,376 --> 00:03:31,794
M.E. says blunt force
trauma to the head.

61
00:03:32,086 --> 00:03:34,213
Puts time of death around midnight
give or take a few hours.

62
00:03:34,839 --> 00:03:39,093
She's wearing a very sensual perfume.
Expensive, with a top note of jasmine.

63
00:03:40,928 --> 00:03:42,263
and she's just shaved her legs.

64
00:03:43,681 --> 00:03:45,057
I think she was going to meet a lover.

65
00:03:45,766 --> 00:03:47,017
Rigsby, you're on trash duty.

66
00:03:47,143 --> 00:03:49,478
Whoever stole the wallet may have
taken the money out and dumped it.

67
00:03:49,603 --> 00:03:51,272
- See if you can find an I.D.
- Copy that.

68
00:03:51,647 --> 00:03:53,274
Jane, let's talk
to the first responders.

69
00:03:53,607 --> 00:03:56,610
Oh, as fun as that might sound I think
I'd rather play some chess.

70
00:03:57,069 --> 00:03:58,112
No offense.

71
00:03:59,321 --> 00:04:00,364
Gentlemen.

72
00:04:09,582 --> 00:04:13,586
Single-malt whiskey.
You have very good taste, uh...

73
00:04:14,253 --> 00:04:17,757
- Walter.
- Walter. Don't mind me.

74
00:04:20,885 --> 00:04:23,637
Uh, no disrespect
but your Grunfeld defense is no match

75
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:25,306
for Walter's classic Spanish game.

76
00:04:26,974 --> 00:04:29,018
If you let me play for you,
I might win your money back.

77
00:04:31,771 --> 00:04:33,647
- Thanks, man.
- Pleasure.

78
00:04:35,024 --> 00:04:36,066
Good luck with that.

79
00:04:41,572 --> 00:04:42,615
Mate in seven.

80
00:04:45,242 --> 00:04:46,786
A sucker born every minute.

81
00:04:48,662 --> 00:04:51,707
- What'd you do with the wallet?
- What wallet?

82
00:04:53,959 --> 00:04:55,377
The one you took
from the dead girl.

83
00:04:57,254 --> 00:04:58,297
What makes you think that?

84
00:05:00,716 --> 00:05:03,219
Because you're not nearly
a good enough chess player

85
00:05:03,344 --> 00:05:05,596
to win enough money
to buy nice scotch like that.

86
00:05:06,388 --> 00:05:09,433
- Oh, no?
- No.

87
00:05:11,894 --> 00:05:14,063
Checkmate. In seven.

88
00:05:15,523 --> 00:05:17,107
You can tell us
about the wallet now

89
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:19,151
or we can find the wallet
with your prints on it

90
00:05:19,276 --> 00:05:21,195
and bring you down to the CBI.
It's your choice.

91
00:05:32,706 --> 00:05:35,709
Aw, yeah.
Who's got next?

92
00:05:46,677 --> 00:05:48,178
Victim's name was Charlotte Coates.

93
00:05:48,303 --> 00:05:49,847
21, goes by Charlie.

94
00:05:49,972 --> 00:05:52,140
Daughter of Congressman Coates
from the 54th district.

95
00:05:52,266 --> 00:05:54,017
And Jane was right.
She was an up-and-coming model.

96
00:05:54,142 --> 00:05:55,185
What else do we know?

97
00:05:55,310 --> 00:05:56,854
About a month ago,
she was pulled over.

98
00:05:56,979 --> 00:05:59,857
Cop found an 8-ball of cocaine on her.
She was arrested for possession.

99
00:06:00,107 --> 00:06:02,860
- Was she charged?
- She pled guilty, agreed to go to rehab.

100
00:06:03,110 --> 00:06:05,195
She was on day 26
of a 30-day program.

101
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:06,780
Place called, uh, Oasis Ranch.

102
00:06:06,905 --> 00:06:09,575
Inpatient. So she checked out of rehab
the night of her death?

103
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:12,411
Snuck out. Park's a drug zone.
Probably went there to score.

104
00:06:12,995 --> 00:06:15,289
- What about the wallet guy?
- No, he was at a homeless shelter

105
00:06:15,414 --> 00:06:17,624
from 7:00 p.m. to 6:00 a.m.
couldn't have done it.

106
00:06:17,958 --> 00:06:20,002
S.F.P.D.'s canvassing
the area for witnesses.

107
00:06:20,669 --> 00:06:22,212
{\an8}- Anything else?
- She didn't have a phone

108
00:06:22,337 --> 00:06:23,589
{\an8}because the rehab
confiscated it

109
00:06:23,714 --> 00:06:25,841
{\an8}so now we don't know if she called
anyone before sneaking out.

110
00:06:25,966 --> 00:06:29,219
{\an8}Before rehab, she sent a bunch
of angry texts to one number.

111
00:06:29,970 --> 00:06:33,223
{\an8}"Screw you for betraying me.
You are a bastard."

112
00:06:33,599 --> 00:06:35,225
- Like that.
- And did you trace the number?

113
00:06:35,350 --> 00:06:40,480
{\an8}Yeah. Belongs to a photographer
called Mo Kaan.

114
00:06:40,772 --> 00:06:43,567
{\an8}All right. Look into him. Jane and I
are gonna go talk to the parents.

115
00:06:43,692 --> 00:06:44,735
{\an8}All right.

116
00:06:46,653 --> 00:06:49,531
{\an8}I want you to understand...
she was a good girl.

117
00:06:49,948 --> 00:06:51,325
{\an8}The drugs were just a phase.

118
00:06:52,534 --> 00:06:53,577
When did she start using?

119
00:06:54,077 --> 00:06:57,080
Um, a few years ago
when she started modeling.

120
00:06:57,789 --> 00:07:01,460
{\an8}As a child, she was always
so shy and sensitive

121
00:07:01,585 --> 00:07:03,670
{\an8}like the volume was turned up
too high in her head.

122
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:08,216
{\an8}I knew modeling was
a tough business and lots of rejection.

123
00:07:09,259 --> 00:07:13,430
{\an8}- I never should have let her do it.
- But you did let her do it

124
00:07:13,722 --> 00:07:15,849
{\an8}and... and the role
of bad cop fell to you.

125
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:17,643
You could say that.

126
00:07:20,062 --> 00:07:21,355
She put us through a lot.

127
00:07:22,230 --> 00:07:25,275
{\an8}You... you were about to mention
something else. What was it?

128
00:07:27,527 --> 00:07:29,363
{\an8}Well, I guess there's no reason
we can't say it now.

129
00:07:29,821 --> 00:07:31,823
A month ago, she stole
a necklace from her mother.

130
00:07:31,949 --> 00:07:35,619
{\an8}- A very expensive ruby necklace.
- Don't say that, Jeffrey.

131
00:07:35,744 --> 00:07:37,621
{\an8}I told you, Charlie
couldn't have done it.

132
00:07:38,038 --> 00:07:40,999
{\an8}Maria was the only person who knew
where I had that necklace hidden.

133
00:07:41,375 --> 00:07:42,417
Maria?

134
00:07:43,377 --> 00:07:46,171
{\an8}She was our maid.
But we had to let her go.

135
00:07:47,714 --> 00:07:48,882
{\an8}Our daughter loved Maria.

136
00:07:49,007 --> 00:07:51,593
{\an8}She would never have let me fire her
for something she didn't do.

137
00:07:52,469 --> 00:07:55,347
{\an8}Can you think of anyone who may
have wanted to hurt your daughter?

138
00:07:58,058 --> 00:08:00,102
{\an8}Who knows, with the people
that she was hanging out with.

139
00:08:02,270 --> 00:08:04,147
{\an8}If you think of anything,
give us a call.

140
00:08:08,568 --> 00:08:12,155
{\an8}Stella, sweetheart...
You look like an angry stick insect.

141
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:15,784
{\an8}Relax. Think of Brazil...
or wherever it is you're from.

142
00:08:15,909 --> 00:08:17,536
{\an8}- Uruguay.
- Uruguay! Fabulous!

143
00:08:17,661 --> 00:08:19,037
{\an8}Work it! Work it!

144
00:08:19,454 --> 00:08:21,331
Yeah, that's right.
That's right.

145
00:08:21,456 --> 00:08:25,335
You're a dirty little Cossack.
Yes, that perestroika!

146
00:08:25,460 --> 00:08:28,755
{\an8}- That's it.
- Mo Kaan. I'm Agent Cho.

147
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,173
{\an8}This is Agent Rigsby, CBI.

148
00:08:30,382 --> 00:08:31,967
{\an8}We are in the middle of something here.
Can I help you?

149
00:08:32,217 --> 00:08:34,094
{\an8}Yeah. Charlie Coates
was murdered last night.

150
00:08:35,721 --> 00:08:38,598
{\an8}My God.
Everyone take five!

151
00:08:41,977 --> 00:08:44,271
Charlie, uh, Charlie was one
of the good ones. Smart kid.

152
00:08:44,563 --> 00:08:47,899
{\an8}- Where were you last night?
- I was at dinner with a client.

153
00:08:48,150 --> 00:08:49,609
{\an8}And then after that,
I was shootin' Estella

154
00:08:49,735 --> 00:08:52,612
{\an8}at some dirty little hotel
in the tenderloin... the Seventh Veil.

155
00:08:52,738 --> 00:08:55,198
- At the corner of Geary and Hyde?
- Yeah.

156
00:08:55,490 --> 00:08:58,452
{\an8}Charlie was killed two blocks from there.
Can anyone confirm your whereabouts?

157
00:08:59,161 --> 00:09:00,871
Sure. Everybody here.

158
00:09:01,705 --> 00:09:04,082
- What were those angry texts about?
- What angry texts?

159
00:09:04,207 --> 00:09:06,501
The ones we found on Charlie's phone
accusing you of betrayal.

160
00:09:07,127 --> 00:09:09,963
Oh. Those.
Nothing, really.

161
00:09:10,630 --> 00:09:12,924
A few weeks ago, Charlie's agent
fired her and she blamed me.

162
00:09:13,050 --> 00:09:15,635
She thought I told him she was
a no-show after partying all night.

163
00:09:16,386 --> 00:09:18,138
- And did you tell him?
- Please.

164
00:09:18,764 --> 00:09:22,017
If I got every crazy, coked-up model fired
I'd have no one to take pictures of.

165
00:09:22,726 --> 00:09:23,977
Speaking of coke,
empty your pockets.

166
00:09:25,479 --> 00:09:26,938
- What?
- Empty your pockets.

167
00:09:27,939 --> 00:09:30,484
Why? This isn't Russia.
You need a reason.

168
00:09:31,359 --> 00:09:33,278
You're acting high,
you're sniffing compulsively

169
00:09:33,403 --> 00:09:36,782
- and you're wearing a coke spoon.
- It's hers.

170
00:09:37,074 --> 00:09:38,867
Slow down, hoss.
We haven't found anything yet.

171
00:09:43,914 --> 00:09:46,541
- Honestly, I was just holding it for her.
- You're under arrest.

172
00:09:55,217 --> 00:09:56,259
Hello.

173
00:09:56,635 --> 00:09:58,970
- I'm Dr. Rubin, executive director.
- Hi.

174
00:09:59,096 --> 00:10:02,307
I'm so glad you're here.
We are all in shock.

175
00:10:03,308 --> 00:10:07,104
- So you... you're a psychiatrist?
- Yes. Stanford Medical School.

176
00:10:07,771 --> 00:10:09,731
Excellent.
That should make things easier.

177
00:10:09,856 --> 00:10:11,942
It's nearly always
the psychiatrist that did it.

178
00:10:12,901 --> 00:10:14,820
Had a bad experience
with therapy, huh?

179
00:10:15,695 --> 00:10:17,364
Were you treating Charlie personally?

180
00:10:17,531 --> 00:10:20,158
No, and I have weekly sessions
with all the inpatients.

181
00:10:20,700 --> 00:10:23,328
I met with Charlie yesterday.

182
00:10:23,662 --> 00:10:26,623
But Joanna Lyle was her primary therapist.
Saw her every day.

183
00:10:27,082 --> 00:10:29,334
You can find her
in the clinical building.

184
00:10:29,835 --> 00:10:32,963
How did Charlie manage to sneak out
and get to the city unnoticed?

185
00:10:33,088 --> 00:10:34,131
Did she have a car?

186
00:10:34,464 --> 00:10:37,759
Uh, no. Patients aren't allowed cars.
It's too much of a temptation.

187
00:10:38,552 --> 00:10:39,678
However, this isn't a prison.

188
00:10:40,345 --> 00:10:42,472
We don't have security cameras
or electric fences.

189
00:10:42,597 --> 00:10:44,975
In fact, we have
so many high-profile patients

190
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:47,602
we're far more worried about keeping
paparazzi and reporters out.

191
00:10:47,936 --> 00:10:49,688
And how was Charlie's treatment going?

192
00:10:50,647 --> 00:10:55,610
Frankly, her spirit was willing
but she didn't want to do the work.

193
00:10:55,735 --> 00:10:59,573
"The work." Who could blame her?
Where were you last night?

194
00:11:00,490 --> 00:11:03,201
I was... here.
Working on my book.

195
00:11:05,537 --> 00:11:08,290
I'm just trying to figure out
who Charlie was sleeping with.

196
00:11:08,957 --> 00:11:11,668
- Was it you?
- Absolutely not.

197
00:11:13,461 --> 00:11:15,088
What makes you think
she was sleeping with anybody?

198
00:11:15,338 --> 00:11:18,049
Because this place is like
a summer camp for drug addicts.

199
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:20,594
It fairly reeks of sex.

200
00:11:21,887 --> 00:11:25,056
Well, we liken early sobriety
to a whack-a-mole game.

201
00:11:25,182 --> 00:11:27,225
You push down one addiction,
and another one pops up.

202
00:11:27,767 --> 00:11:30,562
And even though we have
a strict policy about it

203
00:11:31,396 --> 00:11:35,233
newly sober people
tend to act out sexually.

204
00:11:35,984 --> 00:11:38,278
But I can't tell you
who Charlie was sleeping with.

205
00:11:38,653 --> 00:11:39,696
Why not?

206
00:11:40,322 --> 00:11:42,866
A little thing called
doctor-patient privilege.

207
00:11:43,241 --> 00:11:44,492
Charlie's dead.

208
00:11:44,743 --> 00:11:46,536
You're allowed to share
that information with us.

209
00:11:47,162 --> 00:11:51,416
- And I'm allowed to protect privilege.
- I see.

210
00:11:52,375 --> 00:11:55,295
You're not protecting Charlie.
You're protecting someone else.

211
00:11:56,421 --> 00:12:00,926
Charlie did indeed have a lover here.
They were a patient of yours.

212
00:12:01,843 --> 00:12:04,471
No need to give me a name.
I can figure it out for myself.

213
00:12:05,597 --> 00:12:06,973
Thank you.
You've been very helpful.

214
00:12:08,975 --> 00:12:11,728
We need to talk to this therapist
this Lyle woman.

215
00:12:11,853 --> 00:12:13,813
I'm gonna head back to the office.
I'll have Cho come and meet you here.

216
00:12:13,938 --> 00:12:15,398
Oh, I'm fine. No need for a chaperone.

217
00:12:17,942 --> 00:12:20,403
Hey, Van Pelt.
Could you hang on a sec?

218
00:12:21,988 --> 00:12:23,030
Jane?

219
00:12:25,199 --> 00:12:26,993
- What's up?
- I think I found something big.

220
00:12:27,410 --> 00:12:31,122
Irregular payments from Volker Industries
to a shell corporation.

221
00:12:31,414 --> 00:12:34,041
Listed as consultant fees.
$25,000 each.

222
00:12:34,333 --> 00:12:36,210
Nice work.
Who's cashing the checks?

223
00:12:36,335 --> 00:12:39,005
A guy named Charles Milk.
He's clean as a whistle

224
00:12:39,130 --> 00:12:42,008
but his name came up
in a 2007 case just as a witness.

225
00:12:42,717 --> 00:12:45,428
One of his neighbors
committed suicide. A woman.

226
00:12:45,803 --> 00:12:48,097
Let me guess...
hung herself like Amanda Shaw?

227
00:12:48,473 --> 00:12:49,515
"Exactly."

228
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:51,142
And I got a picture of him.

229
00:12:51,309 --> 00:12:54,228
Matches the sketch of the driver we were
looking for in the Cassie Flood case.

230
00:12:54,479 --> 00:12:56,647
Great work. I'm headed
back to the office now.

231
00:12:56,773 --> 00:12:58,608
Start writing the warrant
for the Milk residence.

232
00:12:58,733 --> 00:13:00,860
- I want to catch him by surprise.
- You got it, boss.

233
00:13:00,985 --> 00:13:02,487
And tell Cho to get over here.

234
00:13:03,863 --> 00:13:05,406
- Dr. Lyle?
- Yes.

235
00:13:05,615 --> 00:13:08,493
Patrick Jane.
With the CBI.

236
00:13:09,619 --> 00:13:11,162
Please, call me Joanna.

237
00:13:11,412 --> 00:13:12,789
And I'm not actually a doctor.

238
00:13:12,914 --> 00:13:15,541
But you were Charlie's
drug counselor, yes?

239
00:13:15,708 --> 00:13:19,545
- Yes. Poor girl. Have a seat.
- Thank you.

240
00:13:19,796 --> 00:13:24,550
Yes, it seems that she, uh...
she broke out to buy some coke.

241
00:13:25,134 --> 00:13:27,386
Is that a... is that
a black mark against you?

242
00:13:28,763 --> 00:13:32,058
As a therapist, I'd like to think
that I can help my patients get sober.

243
00:13:32,183 --> 00:13:34,811
But as a recovering alcoholic

244
00:13:35,394 --> 00:13:38,272
I know I can't make someone
stop before they're ready.

245
00:13:39,273 --> 00:13:41,108
There but for
the Grace of God.

246
00:13:41,651 --> 00:13:43,402
Well, let's leave God
out of it, shall we?

247
00:13:44,195 --> 00:13:46,823
Charlie wasn't exactly
a model patient, was she?

248
00:13:47,657 --> 00:13:49,033
She had a good heart.

249
00:13:49,408 --> 00:13:51,786
She just made it very clear
that she didn't wanna be here.

250
00:13:52,787 --> 00:13:53,955
She wouldn't open up to me.

251
00:13:54,163 --> 00:13:58,501
She, uh, she wouldn't participate
in group... Excuse me...

252
00:13:59,168 --> 00:14:01,337
- Rough night?
- I've been, uh...

253
00:14:02,255 --> 00:14:04,757
I've been on call this week
working overnights

254
00:14:04,882 --> 00:14:07,093
and we discovered that Charlie
was missing from her room

255
00:14:07,218 --> 00:14:11,639
at about 2:00 a.m.
and I've been up ever since.

256
00:14:12,139 --> 00:14:14,392
Running on coffee and cigarettes, huh?

257
00:14:15,059 --> 00:14:19,772
Oh, coffee, yes
but I haven't smoked in years.

258
00:14:20,940 --> 00:14:22,775
Oh. Well, excuse me.

259
00:14:23,985 --> 00:14:27,071
- Could you show me Charlie's room?
- Yes, of course.

260
00:14:27,196 --> 00:14:28,239
Thank you

261
00:14:30,616 --> 00:14:32,410
- What's up?
- Did you fill out the application

262
00:14:32,535 --> 00:14:35,288
- for the Milk warrant?
- I submitted it to Judge Davis, but...

263
00:14:36,539 --> 00:14:38,499
- What?
- It's Volker. He's here.

264
00:14:47,174 --> 00:14:50,511
- Agent Lisbon.
- What do you want, Mr. Volker?

265
00:14:52,513 --> 00:14:54,891
Brass tacks.
I like that.

266
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:57,184
As I'm sure you're aware

267
00:14:57,935 --> 00:15:01,022
I run a very successful business
worth billions of dollars.

268
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:03,482
You wanna know my secret?

269
00:15:05,484 --> 00:15:08,696
Transparency.
Honesty.

270
00:15:09,739 --> 00:15:11,324
Open lines of communication.

271
00:15:12,575 --> 00:15:13,743
It's the way I do business.

272
00:15:15,995 --> 00:15:17,038
What's your point?

273
00:15:17,788 --> 00:15:22,960
If you wanted my financial records
all you had to do was ask for them.

274
00:15:24,921 --> 00:15:28,633
I got nothing to hide.
You found nothing, right?

275
00:15:29,467 --> 00:15:32,053
Why? Is there something
you're worried about?

276
00:15:33,804 --> 00:15:34,847
Next time...

277
00:15:37,016 --> 00:15:38,059
Just ask.

278
00:15:40,728 --> 00:15:41,771
You look good.

279
00:15:43,356 --> 00:15:44,398
You've been working out.

280
00:15:46,192 --> 00:15:47,318
Get out of my office.

281
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,947
Have a lovely day,
Agent Lisbon.

282
00:16:15,346 --> 00:16:17,390
Hey, Cho.
You're freaking out the guests.

283
00:16:17,932 --> 00:16:21,602
- Just relax with the copness.
- I'm relaxed.

284
00:16:29,819 --> 00:16:30,861
Here we are.

285
00:16:31,862 --> 00:16:32,905
Susie?

286
00:16:33,364 --> 00:16:37,201
- Hey. How you holding up?
- Okay, I guess.

287
00:16:37,868 --> 00:16:38,911
Shouldn't you be in group?

288
00:16:39,787 --> 00:16:43,624
You should go. Talk about
what happened with Charlie, your feelings.

289
00:16:44,291 --> 00:16:47,336
- Hi. You were her roommate?
- Yeah. Who are you?

290
00:16:48,462 --> 00:16:51,173
Susie, these guys
are here with the CBI

291
00:16:51,382 --> 00:16:53,259
to investigate
what happened with Charlie.

292
00:16:53,592 --> 00:16:54,969
That's Patrick Jane.
I'm Agent Cho.

293
00:16:56,303 --> 00:17:01,517
- Jane as in Austen or Mansfield?
- Austen.

294
00:17:02,643 --> 00:17:07,857
- What are you here for?
- Coke. Speed. Some pills.

295
00:17:08,774 --> 00:17:09,817
Ambitious.

296
00:17:10,443 --> 00:17:13,529
- So Charlie was a tea drinker?
- No. Those are mine.

297
00:17:14,113 --> 00:17:15,531
Did you see Charlie
sneaking out last night?

298
00:17:16,073 --> 00:17:19,285
Yes. I didn't think anything of it.
She sneaks out all the time.

299
00:17:19,785 --> 00:17:21,662
Susie, you should have reported it.

300
00:17:21,787 --> 00:17:24,415
- It's a major breach of the honor system.
- I know, I know.

301
00:17:25,458 --> 00:17:27,251
I'm gonna have to tell
Dr. Rubin about it.

302
00:17:28,210 --> 00:17:30,713
- Come on. Are you serious?
- What time did she sneak out?

303
00:17:31,213 --> 00:17:33,799
I don't know.
Around 10:00, I guess.

304
00:17:34,467 --> 00:17:35,509
You know
where she was going?

305
00:17:36,343 --> 00:17:37,762
I have no idea.
We weren't that close.

306
00:17:39,263 --> 00:17:40,306
Jasmine.

307
00:17:41,891 --> 00:17:45,144
Dr. Lyle, where is that group therapy
session going down?

308
00:17:45,895 --> 00:17:46,937
Uh, just down the hall.

309
00:17:48,272 --> 00:17:49,482
- Thank you.
- Thanks.

310
00:17:51,776 --> 00:17:54,028
My name is Armando
and I'm an addict.

311
00:17:54,737 --> 00:17:55,863
Hi, Armando.

312
00:17:55,988 --> 00:17:58,032
But I mean, not like you guys.
No offense.

313
00:17:58,657 --> 00:18:01,952
My life's a party.
Champagne. Fine women.

314
00:18:03,788 --> 00:18:05,623
Translation... light beer
and cheap hookers.

315
00:18:05,831 --> 00:18:08,626
- Hey, now.
- Yo. Why the hostility, man?

316
00:18:09,376 --> 00:18:10,795
I'm only being honest here, right?

317
00:18:11,754 --> 00:18:13,672
See this watch?
Girls gave this stuff to me.

318
00:18:14,632 --> 00:18:18,636
And that's my problem.
I'm addicted to women.

319
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:22,389
Excuse me. Uh, sorry to interrupt
just when it was getting good.

320
00:18:22,807 --> 00:18:25,309
My name is Patrick Jane.
I'm a consultant with the CBI.

321
00:18:25,434 --> 00:18:27,603
We're investigating
the murder of Charlie Coates.

322
00:18:28,020 --> 00:18:31,565
- And, I need your help.
- Okay.

323
00:18:32,316 --> 00:18:33,567
You may not think...

324
00:18:35,236 --> 00:18:39,365
You know anything of interest but
the subconscious mind knows a lot more.

325
00:18:39,907 --> 00:18:42,159
That's why I'm gonna ask
you all, as a group

326
00:18:42,576 --> 00:18:45,538
to close your eyes
and picture Charlie.

327
00:18:47,456 --> 00:18:51,627
Uh, I want you to think about
the last time you saw Charlie.

328
00:18:54,046 --> 00:18:55,840
Every detail counts.

329
00:18:57,049 --> 00:18:59,927
Her laugh.
The color of her eyes.

330
00:19:01,637 --> 00:19:02,680
Her perfume.

331
00:19:04,181 --> 00:19:05,558
Every little detail.

332
00:19:06,517 --> 00:19:09,061
Okay. Thank you.

333
00:19:09,603 --> 00:19:10,771
Now if you'll open your eyes.

334
00:19:13,232 --> 00:19:17,778
It appears you two are
intimately familiar with her scent.

335
00:19:17,903 --> 00:19:19,947
But Charlie doesn't strike me
as a two-timer.

336
00:19:20,072 --> 00:19:24,076
So one of you was the boyfriend
and the other one, well, he was hoping.

337
00:19:24,410 --> 00:19:27,163
Let me see. You seem
to have a way with women.

338
00:19:27,371 --> 00:19:32,626
I would guess that Charlie may have
been drawn to your machismo.

339
00:19:34,086 --> 00:19:38,257
- She found you irresistible.
- Maybe. But you know.

340
00:19:40,301 --> 00:19:42,261
- You were sleeping together?
- No.

341
00:19:43,804 --> 00:19:47,266
Uh, you... you're lying.
You were sleeping together. I can tell.

342
00:19:47,391 --> 00:19:48,767
- No. No.
- Yes.

343
00:19:49,101 --> 00:19:50,728
I mean, I tried,
of course, but...

344
00:19:50,895 --> 00:19:53,063
- You bastard!
- And here comes the real boyfriend.

345
00:19:57,693 --> 00:19:59,278
Uh, just back away there.
I was just kidding.

346
00:19:59,403 --> 00:20:00,905
He wasn't actually
sleeping with her.

347
00:20:01,030 --> 00:20:02,740
Just... Cho!
Cho!

348
00:20:02,865 --> 00:20:04,241
I didn't even touch her!
Get off me!

349
00:20:06,118 --> 00:20:07,161
Get off me, man!

350
00:20:13,297 --> 00:20:14,340
Phoenix Bell.

351
00:20:15,008 --> 00:20:16,050
Your father's Anton Bell.

352
00:20:16,175 --> 00:20:17,844
Starred in those action movies
back in the '80s, right?

353
00:20:18,761 --> 00:20:20,972
And who's your father?
Is he relevant also?

354
00:20:23,016 --> 00:20:25,977
Point taken. Tell me
about you and Charlie.

355
00:20:28,104 --> 00:20:31,149
She was funny
and strong and... real.

356
00:20:32,483 --> 00:20:33,526
But fragile, too.

357
00:20:34,736 --> 00:20:36,320
Not like these girls
I meet in L.A.

358
00:20:37,780 --> 00:20:40,158
I know the doctors say she didn't want
to get better but she did.

359
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:42,535
She made me want
to get better, too.

360
00:20:42,952 --> 00:20:44,162
We talked
to your roommate, Phoenix.

361
00:20:44,954 --> 00:20:47,832
He says you snuck out of your room
at 11:00 on the night Charlie died

362
00:20:47,957 --> 00:20:49,792
and didn't come home
until 1:00 in the morning. Where were you?

363
00:20:51,085 --> 00:20:52,795
We had this spot where
we'd meet out in the desert.

364
00:20:53,629 --> 00:20:56,424
That night we were supposed to hook up
at 11:00 but Charlie didn't show.

365
00:20:56,883 --> 00:20:59,427
- What'd you do?
- I freaked out.

366
00:21:00,678 --> 00:21:04,140
I thought that she was over me
or she had relapsed or something.

367
00:21:05,558 --> 00:21:09,437
- So I took a drive.
- You have a car?

368
00:21:11,606 --> 00:21:14,567
My dad pulled a few strings got me
some extra privileges. Whatever.

369
00:21:14,859 --> 00:21:17,987
- Where'd you go?
- Just around.

370
00:21:19,697 --> 00:21:20,740
Then I went to a liquor store.

371
00:21:22,992 --> 00:21:24,035
You get loaded?

372
00:21:24,869 --> 00:21:27,330
No. I wanted to.

373
00:21:28,706 --> 00:21:30,833
- Anyone see you there?
- No.

374
00:21:33,127 --> 00:21:34,170
But you have to believe me.

375
00:21:35,171 --> 00:21:38,966
All the bad things I've done in my life
I would never hurt Charlie.

376
00:21:39,092 --> 00:21:40,676
Right. Can you think
of anyone who would?

377
00:21:42,762 --> 00:21:45,681
I don't know. A few nights ago,
we were in our spot

378
00:21:45,807 --> 00:21:47,600
and we saw somebody
spying on us from far away.

379
00:21:48,726 --> 00:21:51,479
- You went after them?
- Yeah, but I didn't even get close.

380
00:21:55,858 --> 00:21:59,862
If she would have just come that night
maybe I could have helped her.

381
00:22:05,660 --> 00:22:09,038
Phoenix had access to a car.
He has no alibi for the time of death.

382
00:22:10,164 --> 00:22:12,500
And his story about someone
spying on them is sketchy.

383
00:22:12,667 --> 00:22:13,709
You think he made it up?

384
00:22:13,835 --> 00:22:15,670
No, someone was watching
Phoenix and Charlie.

385
00:22:15,795 --> 00:22:17,130
The question is who?

386
00:22:17,255 --> 00:22:19,340
Son of a movie star,
daughter of a politician.

387
00:22:19,590 --> 00:22:21,551
- Could have been the paparazzi.
- What about Armando?

388
00:22:21,676 --> 00:22:23,302
No, he had an alibi
for the night of the murder.

389
00:22:23,427 --> 00:22:25,304
His roommate was up all night
listening to him snore.

390
00:22:25,555 --> 00:22:27,265
Rigs, where are we at
with the photographer?

391
00:22:27,390 --> 00:22:29,934
- He's been in holding overnight. Ok
- Good, go talk to him.

392
00:22:30,059 --> 00:22:32,603
Find out where Phoenix was
between 11:00 and 1:00.

393
00:22:32,728 --> 00:22:34,272
We'll hold on to him
for as long as we can.

394
00:22:34,814 --> 00:22:36,357
I have an idea.
I'm gonna go back to rehab.

395
00:22:36,482 --> 00:22:38,317
- You wanna come with?
- I've got a hit on Volker.

396
00:22:38,442 --> 00:22:41,154
I think I found his enforcer.
He's a guy named Charles Milk.

397
00:22:41,279 --> 00:22:42,738
I'm waiting to get
a warrant on his residence.

398
00:22:42,864 --> 00:22:43,906
Bravo.

399
00:22:44,240 --> 00:22:47,618
There's no way this guy is as smart
or as careful as Volker. I can turn him.

400
00:22:47,743 --> 00:22:50,830
Excellent police work, Lisbon.
I admire your pluck.

401
00:22:51,455 --> 00:22:54,375
- I hear a "but"
- No "but." I'm just a little worried

402
00:22:54,500 --> 00:22:55,877
that he's inside your head.
And believe me

403
00:22:56,002 --> 00:22:58,087
that's not a good road to go down.
Bad neighborhood.

404
00:22:58,337 --> 00:23:00,423
I think you can understand,
I don't really have a choice.

405
00:23:00,548 --> 00:23:01,966
Well, yeah, I can
certainly understand that.

406
00:23:02,091 --> 00:23:05,303
I just... I...
I want you to be careful.

407
00:23:07,138 --> 00:23:09,599
He may be powerful,
but he is not invincible.

408
00:23:09,724 --> 00:23:11,517
- And he's not in my head.
- I hope not.

409
00:23:11,684 --> 00:23:12,727
If you need my help,
let me know.

410
00:23:12,852 --> 00:23:15,354
- No, thanks. This one's mine.
- Yeah, you got this.

411
00:23:16,272 --> 00:23:17,857
Hey, boss, I just got a call.

412
00:23:17,982 --> 00:23:19,692
The judge denied
the search warrant for Milk.

413
00:23:23,029 --> 00:23:25,364
- Excuse me...
- Judge Davis, I just need a minute.

414
00:23:25,489 --> 00:23:26,532
I'm late for an appointment.

415
00:23:26,657 --> 00:23:29,702
I need you to reconsider signing
the Charles Milk warrant, please.

416
00:23:30,077 --> 00:23:32,205
- It's not going to happen.
- Why not?

417
00:23:32,330 --> 00:23:34,916
We have clear evidence of payment
for the commission of murder.

418
00:23:35,374 --> 00:23:36,709
Spare me the hyperbole.

419
00:23:36,834 --> 00:23:39,712
You have murky evidence
of payments for consulting.

420
00:23:39,837 --> 00:23:42,590
Frankly, we had less before
you signed the last warrant.

421
00:23:42,715 --> 00:23:44,467
What happened
between then and now?

422
00:23:45,509 --> 00:23:46,552
Did he get to you?

423
00:23:47,136 --> 00:23:48,554
I'm gonna pretend
I didn't just hear that.

424
00:23:50,181 --> 00:23:51,224
He did, didn't he?

425
00:23:52,600 --> 00:23:55,228
That's why he came to see me,
to show he wasn't scared.

426
00:23:55,353 --> 00:23:57,647
You know what? I'm not gonna sit here
and listen to your accusations

427
00:23:57,772 --> 00:24:01,234
nor am I gonna get dragged any further
into your personal vendetta.

428
00:24:02,610 --> 00:24:05,238
Now... If you will excuse me.

429
00:24:15,248 --> 00:24:17,583
I bet you loved
to watch Charlie beg.

430
00:24:19,377 --> 00:24:20,461
I don't know
what you're getting at.

431
00:24:20,753 --> 00:24:22,046
Well, you can't seem
to stay out of trouble.

432
00:24:22,463 --> 00:24:26,842
- Underage girls, drugs.
- It's not... my fault.

433
00:24:27,218 --> 00:24:28,261
You know what I think?

434
00:24:28,719 --> 00:24:31,138
I think Charlie was gonna meet you
the night she snuck out of rehab.

435
00:24:32,515 --> 00:24:35,017
She wanted drugs, you wanted sex
things got a little weird.

436
00:24:35,351 --> 00:24:36,602
You didn't mean
to hurt her, but you did.

437
00:24:37,186 --> 00:24:38,479
So you took
her body to the park

438
00:24:38,604 --> 00:24:39,939
made it look
like a random drug deal.

439
00:24:40,064 --> 00:24:42,108
- No...
- Just another model with a coke habit.

440
00:24:42,233 --> 00:24:44,026
No. None of...none...
none of that happened.

441
00:24:44,151 --> 00:24:48,281
No. That's not true, okay?
I don't...

442
00:24:50,074 --> 00:24:51,617
I don't wanna be here
anymore now.

443
00:24:51,951 --> 00:24:54,161
I wanna go home now, please.

444
00:24:57,164 --> 00:24:58,332
Hello, Grace.
Do you have anything?

445
00:24:58,749 --> 00:25:00,710
I set an alert
for the name Phoenix Bell

446
00:25:00,835 --> 00:25:04,672
and I'm checking all social media
and gossip sites. Nothing so far.

447
00:25:05,089 --> 00:25:06,632
But I've learned a lot
about Lindsay Lohan.

448
00:25:07,758 --> 00:25:09,969
- Can you try again, please?
- "Sure. Give me a minute."

449
00:25:11,429 --> 00:25:15,141
- Refill, please, Luis?
- Another rough one?

450
00:25:15,725 --> 00:25:17,810
Oh, these overnights
will be the death of me.

451
00:25:18,686 --> 00:25:21,063
But I shouldn't complain.
I live halfway to Reno.

452
00:25:21,188 --> 00:25:23,858
So at least it's a break
from the commute, right?

453
00:25:25,526 --> 00:25:26,694
- Well, cheers.
- Cheers.

454
00:25:26,861 --> 00:25:28,237
Are you there, Jane?
I found something.

455
00:25:28,446 --> 00:25:29,488
Excuse me.

456
00:25:29,739 --> 00:25:31,657
Uh, yes, Grace.
Sorry. Go on.

457
00:25:31,949 --> 00:25:34,910
The gossip site Rumorhound
just re-tweeted this...

458
00:25:35,202 --> 00:25:37,830
"Phoenix Bell,
son of movie star Anton Bell"

459
00:25:37,955 --> 00:25:39,707
"suspect in murder
of his girlfriend."

460
00:25:39,999 --> 00:25:42,752
"The two met at infamous rehab
Oasis Ranch."

461
00:25:43,544 --> 00:25:46,797
Who was the, uh, tweeterer...

462
00:25:47,173 --> 00:25:48,758
Someone named Margaret Hammersby.

463
00:25:49,342 --> 00:25:51,302
- She's a journalist.
- Excellent.

464
00:26:02,730 --> 00:26:03,773
Hi, Susie.

465
00:26:04,815 --> 00:26:06,359
Could I bother you
for a cup of tea?

466
00:26:07,818 --> 00:26:10,780
- Sure. Come on in.
- Thank you.

467
00:26:14,325 --> 00:26:17,536
- Would you like chamomile or mint?
- Chamomile, please.

468
00:26:19,455 --> 00:26:22,458
- Water's hot. There you go.
- That's very kind.

469
00:26:23,167 --> 00:26:25,044
- Thanks, Margaret.
- You're welcome.

470
00:26:30,216 --> 00:26:31,258
Oh, fudge.

471
00:26:34,804 --> 00:26:36,180
Your real name is
Margaret Hammersby.

472
00:26:36,305 --> 00:26:38,682
- You're a journalist.
- How did you find out?

473
00:26:39,058 --> 00:26:42,061
Well, only a journalist would ask
the correct spelling of my name.

474
00:26:42,603 --> 00:26:44,230
"Mansfield." Please.

475
00:26:44,772 --> 00:26:47,233
And what self-respecting speed
freak drinks herbal tea?

476
00:26:48,234 --> 00:26:50,486
I have to be undercover
in order to get this story.

477
00:26:50,861 --> 00:26:53,697
Woodward and Bernstein
you are not, my dear.

478
00:26:54,073 --> 00:26:58,160
You're tweeting trivia about celebrities...
sons of celebrities...

479
00:26:59,578 --> 00:27:03,958
- like Phoenix Bell.
- That's a big scoop. I had to tweet it.

480
00:27:04,125 --> 00:27:05,709
That was you spying
on them the other night.

481
00:27:06,544 --> 00:27:08,337
I only followed them out
that one time.

482
00:27:08,462 --> 00:27:11,132
I swear, I have no idea where
she was going the night she died.

483
00:27:11,382 --> 00:27:13,759
She didn't really open up
to me. Not really.

484
00:27:15,177 --> 00:27:17,972
She got emotional when
she got this card from her parents.

485
00:27:19,306 --> 00:27:22,852
- This card?
- Yeah. She cried like a baby.

486
00:27:23,561 --> 00:27:24,645
"We're so proud of you."

487
00:27:26,814 --> 00:27:27,857
When did she get this?

488
00:27:29,024 --> 00:27:31,610
Three days ago.
The day before she died.

489
00:27:32,695 --> 00:27:35,656
After she got the card
she started writing this letter in Spanish

490
00:27:35,781 --> 00:27:37,616
but then she got frustrated
and ripped it up.

491
00:27:38,576 --> 00:27:40,995
And then you promptly dug it
out of the trash, didn't you?

492
00:27:42,204 --> 00:27:44,665
Yes, I did.
But I don't speak Spanish.

493
00:27:44,790 --> 00:27:46,876
The only thing I can remember
is "lo siento."

494
00:27:47,126 --> 00:27:48,294
That means "I'm sorry."

495
00:27:49,128 --> 00:27:51,255
Excellent.
You've been very helpful.

496
00:27:51,964 --> 00:27:53,340
You're not gonna
blow my cover, are you?

497
00:27:53,757 --> 00:27:55,926
Well, that's for me to know
and for you to find out.

498
00:27:59,096 --> 00:28:00,306
You know, you don't
have to stick around.

499
00:28:00,431 --> 00:28:03,434
- I can meet you back at CBI.
- I'm supposed to stay with you.

500
00:28:03,934 --> 00:28:05,853
What kind of trouble
am I gonna get in at rehab?

501
00:29:04,909 --> 00:29:07,871
The photographer asked for a lawyer.
I think he might be good for this.

502
00:29:07,996 --> 00:29:10,874
- He's more than just ironically pervy.
- Agreed.

503
00:29:11,724 --> 00:29:13,476
And the sexual motive
is always a good one.

504
00:29:13,726 --> 00:29:15,854
But, uh, you can let him go.
Phoenix, too.

505
00:29:17,021 --> 00:29:19,357
- You have better motive?
- Uh, yeah.

506
00:29:19,482 --> 00:29:22,527
An extremely valuable ruby
necklace is a pretty good one.

507
00:29:23,236 --> 00:29:24,571
But we don't have any evidence

508
00:29:24,696 --> 00:29:27,282
that Charlie actually stole
the necklace from her mother.

509
00:29:27,740 --> 00:29:29,784
She was broke.
Of course she stole it.

510
00:29:29,909 --> 00:29:31,411
Then she got that card
from her parents

511
00:29:31,536 --> 00:29:33,037
and she started
to feel bad about it.

512
00:29:33,454 --> 00:29:35,957
- Where are you getting all this?
- The undercover journalist told me

513
00:29:36,082 --> 00:29:38,168
that Charlie started
writing a letter in Spanish

514
00:29:38,293 --> 00:29:40,712
- to say "lo siento"
- Which means "I'm sorry"?

515
00:29:40,837 --> 00:29:43,173
Yes. She was trying
to make amends with Maria

516
00:29:43,298 --> 00:29:45,049
the maid that was fired
for stealing the necklace.

517
00:29:45,175 --> 00:29:47,302
But we never found the necklace
in Charlie's apartment

518
00:29:47,427 --> 00:29:49,470
or her room
at the Oasis Ranch.

519
00:29:49,721 --> 00:29:52,599
Because the killer
stole it from her.

520
00:29:54,267 --> 00:29:57,896
Okay, wait. If Charlie did steal
the necklace and felt guilty about it

521
00:29:58,021 --> 00:29:59,689
don't you think she would have
confided in someone?

522
00:29:59,939 --> 00:30:01,232
Yes, that's exactly what I think.

523
00:30:02,358 --> 00:30:03,401
Hello?

524
00:30:04,319 --> 00:30:05,361
Dr. Rubin.

525
00:30:06,696 --> 00:30:07,739
What's that?

526
00:30:09,824 --> 00:30:12,452
Well, thank you for letting us know.
We'll be there shortly.

527
00:30:14,037 --> 00:30:16,331
Apparently there was a rash
of robberies earlier today.

528
00:30:16,456 --> 00:30:18,541
A lot of the patients
got their valuables stolen.

529
00:30:19,334 --> 00:30:20,376
Imagine that.

530
00:30:20,501 --> 00:30:22,128
They're gonna search
the rooms to find the thief.

531
00:30:22,420 --> 00:30:23,963
Oh, my. We should
head out there, Lisbon.

532
00:30:24,339 --> 00:30:26,466
I'm sorry. I can't.
I'll meet you there later.

533
00:30:28,968 --> 00:30:30,011
So mysterious.

534
00:30:31,471 --> 00:30:34,641
Let me see... Thursday night.
You're going to play poker.

535
00:30:35,141 --> 00:30:37,685
Get one of those muckety-mucks
to sign off on your warrant.

536
00:30:37,810 --> 00:30:38,853
It's worth a shot.

537
00:30:39,395 --> 00:30:41,064
If this doesn't work, I don't
know what I'm gonna do.

538
00:30:41,564 --> 00:30:43,024
Eh, we'll think of something.
Good luck.

539
00:30:46,986 --> 00:30:48,321
Let's see what you got, Senator.

540
00:30:50,657 --> 00:30:51,699
Full house.

541
00:30:54,035 --> 00:30:55,078
You've bled me dry.

542
00:30:57,038 --> 00:30:58,081
I need a drink.

543
00:31:03,878 --> 00:31:06,506
Judge Manchester.
Excuse me, sir.

544
00:31:06,631 --> 00:31:08,132
I need to discuss
something with you.

545
00:31:08,258 --> 00:31:09,842
I'm in no mood, Agent Lisbon.

546
00:31:09,968 --> 00:31:13,179
I don't want to bother you,
I hate to but this is important.

547
00:31:13,304 --> 00:31:14,347
Let me guess...

548
00:31:14,806 --> 00:31:17,183
Tommy Volker
and the Charles Milk warrant.

549
00:31:17,308 --> 00:31:18,351
You heard.

550
00:31:19,394 --> 00:31:21,896
Judge Davis mentioned something
about your little visit.

551
00:31:22,939 --> 00:31:27,777
- She said you had some nerve.
- I was upset. I spoke in haste.

552
00:31:28,695 --> 00:31:30,196
No need to apologize to me.

553
00:31:30,446 --> 00:31:32,657
Oh, I don't want to apologize.
Davis was wrong.

554
00:31:32,782 --> 00:31:35,785
I mean, Volker is a sociopath,
and he needs to be taken down.

555
00:31:36,244 --> 00:31:37,996
If not by me,
then by somebody else.

556
00:31:38,830 --> 00:31:41,332
Sometimes you are
childishly naive, Teresa.

557
00:31:41,874 --> 00:31:44,252
That might be so, but which side
would you rather be on?

558
00:31:44,877 --> 00:31:48,214
- Childish naivete, or defeated cynicism?
- Ouch.

559
00:31:49,090 --> 00:31:52,969
Please, sign the Milk warrant, Judge.
It's legit.

560
00:31:53,886 --> 00:31:55,555
The only reason not to is fear.

561
00:32:00,351 --> 00:32:02,395
Doctor.
We're here to help you search.

562
00:32:02,979 --> 00:32:05,315
Do you think the robberies could have
something to do with this case?

563
00:32:05,606 --> 00:32:07,692
Maybe. We won't know
until we search the room first.

564
00:32:07,859 --> 00:32:09,652
Well, this isn't the first time
we've had things stolen.

565
00:32:09,777 --> 00:32:11,362
It's quite common, in fact.

566
00:32:11,529 --> 00:32:13,865
It's another way for addicts
to act out in early sobriety.

567
00:32:13,990 --> 00:32:15,867
You and your fancy diagnoses.

568
00:32:15,992 --> 00:32:17,869
When people want stuff,
they take it.

569
00:32:17,994 --> 00:32:19,037
It's as simple as that.

570
00:32:19,162 --> 00:32:21,622
Now let's get to searching, shall we?
This place isn't gonna search itself.

571
00:32:32,717 --> 00:32:33,760
- What are you doing?
- What?

572
00:32:34,969 --> 00:32:36,012
Put it back.

573
00:32:37,680 --> 00:32:38,723
Put it back.

574
00:32:39,223 --> 00:32:42,226
What are you talking about?
I'm trying to search here.

575
00:32:42,352 --> 00:32:43,853
- Could you just be a little quiet?
- Excuse me. Excuse me.

576
00:32:43,978 --> 00:32:45,021
What's going on?

577
00:32:45,271 --> 00:32:49,650
I'm sorry, Doctor. Jane's had some
problems, uh... taking stuff.

578
00:32:50,526 --> 00:32:53,029
Oh. Well, that's the first
I've ever heard of that.

579
00:32:53,196 --> 00:32:54,614
Well, in that case,
let's empty your pocket.

580
00:32:54,739 --> 00:32:55,782
No, I will not.

581
00:32:55,907 --> 00:32:58,368
Don't make this any worse than it is.
Empty your pockets right now.

582
00:33:02,663 --> 00:33:03,790
Wow. That's...

583
00:33:06,667 --> 00:33:08,086
Can't believe I couldn't
feel that in there.

584
00:33:12,006 --> 00:33:14,384
That's not mine. I didn't...
That's... that's not my wallet.

585
00:33:14,509 --> 00:33:16,886
I think we should reconvene
in my office for a little chat.

586
00:33:17,303 --> 00:33:19,680
Keith, Marvin, would you escort
Mr. Jane to the office?

587
00:33:19,806 --> 00:33:20,848
Watch the suit.

588
00:33:23,559 --> 00:33:24,936
I got here as soon as I could.

589
00:33:25,937 --> 00:33:28,523
Kleptomania is a disease,
and you need help.

590
00:33:28,648 --> 00:33:29,857
Oh, please.

591
00:33:30,191 --> 00:33:31,734
I've told him that,
but he won't listen.

592
00:33:32,527 --> 00:33:35,738
It's not your fault.
There is nothing to be ashamed of.

593
00:33:36,030 --> 00:33:37,156
Yeah, see,
the last thing I need

594
00:33:37,281 --> 00:33:39,951
is some new age nonsense
rattling around inside my head.

595
00:33:40,076 --> 00:33:42,453
Jane, I don't think you understand
how much trouble you're in.

596
00:33:42,787 --> 00:33:44,038
- They could press charges.
- No, hang on.

597
00:33:44,163 --> 00:33:45,415
We're not there yet.
We're not there yet.

598
00:33:45,540 --> 00:33:48,418
- I wanna hear from Mr. Jane.
- You're not even a real doctor.

599
00:33:48,751 --> 00:33:51,504
- I don't have to talk to you.
- Jane...

600
00:33:53,089 --> 00:33:55,675
It couldn't hurt.
Please?

601
00:33:57,176 --> 00:33:58,219
Okay.

602
00:33:59,762 --> 00:34:02,640
I like to take stuff,
and I'm good at it.

603
00:34:03,724 --> 00:34:05,393
I don't see
what the big deal is.

604
00:34:05,893 --> 00:34:07,562
Well, this behavior
doesn't come from nowhere.

605
00:34:09,355 --> 00:34:10,398
No. You're right.

606
00:34:10,815 --> 00:34:13,526
When I was 10, my father
taught me to pick pockets

607
00:34:13,651 --> 00:34:15,403
and we, uh, knocked off
a few houses.

608
00:34:15,528 --> 00:34:19,198
And, uh, and then we...
moved on to a couple of banks.

609
00:34:19,323 --> 00:34:21,826
But I didn't...
the banks was not my cup of tea.

610
00:34:21,951 --> 00:34:26,038
I don't like the banks 'cause of the anxiety
and the screaming and all the hysteria.

611
00:34:26,164 --> 00:34:27,373
It doesn't sit well with me.

612
00:34:29,417 --> 00:34:34,839
So subconsciously, you're still trying
to please your father, hmm?

613
00:34:41,053 --> 00:34:42,096
Yeah.

614
00:34:44,807 --> 00:34:45,975
Yeah. That's, uh...

615
00:34:50,688 --> 00:34:53,566
- How do you do that? That is uncanny.
- Jane...

616
00:34:58,112 --> 00:34:59,155
Hello, Cho?

617
00:35:01,991 --> 00:35:06,037
A ruby necklace?
Really? Thanks.

618
00:35:07,622 --> 00:35:10,208
They just found an expensive
ruby necklace in your car.

619
00:35:10,750 --> 00:35:12,084
You wanna explain
how it got there?

620
00:35:14,170 --> 00:35:15,213
Not really.

621
00:35:15,338 --> 00:35:17,089
Thank you.
But this is a police matter now.

622
00:35:17,215 --> 00:35:19,842
If you two wouldn't mind giving me
a moment alone with Jane.

623
00:35:19,967 --> 00:35:21,385
Yes, of course.
We'll leave you alone.

624
00:35:23,846 --> 00:35:25,765
You definitely should
continue therapy.

625
00:35:27,141 --> 00:35:30,353
- I... I can make a referral.
- Thanks, Doc.

626
00:35:31,354 --> 00:35:34,023
I mean, I...
I feel better already.

627
00:35:35,024 --> 00:35:36,067
Thank you.

628
00:36:07,820 --> 00:36:08,863
Busted.

629
00:36:12,491 --> 00:36:13,576
You're in massive debt.

630
00:36:14,201 --> 00:36:18,372
Cash advances, credit cards
home equity loans.

631
00:36:19,081 --> 00:36:21,625
What is it?
Craps? Roulette?

632
00:36:23,127 --> 00:36:26,505
Those are for suckers.
I have skill.

633
00:36:27,298 --> 00:36:28,340
Blackjack then.

634
00:36:30,676 --> 00:36:31,719
How did you know?

635
00:36:32,052 --> 00:36:33,095
Well, you told Jane you didn't smoke

636
00:36:33,220 --> 00:36:35,598
and yet the inside of your office
smelled like a casino ashtray.

637
00:36:36,348 --> 00:36:38,350
And you referred to home
as being "halfway to Reno."

638
00:36:40,019 --> 00:36:45,232
It started... years ago,
after I stopped drinking.

639
00:36:46,942 --> 00:36:52,114
Good, clean fun, right?
But it got out of control.

640
00:36:53,282 --> 00:36:56,035
I lost my house

641
00:36:58,037 --> 00:37:01,999
burned through my kid's college fund
and I still couldn't stop.

642
00:37:02,875 --> 00:37:03,918
How did you pay for it?

643
00:37:06,045 --> 00:37:09,715
I started borrowing money
from people. Bad people.

644
00:37:10,841 --> 00:37:12,051
They were going to hurt me.

645
00:37:13,344 --> 00:37:15,471
So you heard about the necklace
and you saw a way out.

646
00:37:16,597 --> 00:37:20,392
Charlie had this... this...
moment of clarity

647
00:37:21,018 --> 00:37:23,354
after she got that stupid card.
She, uh...

648
00:37:24,521 --> 00:37:27,441
came into therapy,
told me she had stolen the necklace.

649
00:37:29,360 --> 00:37:32,112
She had tried to sell it but she didn't have
the right connections.

650
00:37:33,739 --> 00:37:35,491
And then she wanted to give it
back to her parents.

651
00:37:36,492 --> 00:37:37,952
And you were the only person
she told.

652
00:37:38,702 --> 00:37:41,997
She said she wanted
to make amends, but come on.

653
00:37:42,331 --> 00:37:44,708
It was a quarter of a million dollars.
I needed it.

654
00:37:48,212 --> 00:37:53,342
I convinced her to sneak out
go back to her place to get the jewels.

655
00:37:58,514 --> 00:38:03,686
"I said that she should give them back
to her parents at her 30-day chip ceremony"

656
00:38:03,811 --> 00:38:06,355
"that I was... proud of her."

657
00:38:12,319 --> 00:38:16,657
I pulled over, told her I thought
I had a flat.

658
00:38:19,994 --> 00:38:22,371
"I'd heard about that park
from some of my other patients"

659
00:38:22,663 --> 00:38:24,415
"that it was a place to score."

660
00:38:33,549 --> 00:38:35,301
I knew how it would look.

661
00:38:44,768 --> 00:38:45,811
So you killed her

662
00:38:46,645 --> 00:38:49,064
and you took the necklace
back to Oasis Ranch

663
00:38:50,983 --> 00:38:54,194
and you let her parents believe
that she died buying drugs.

664
00:38:56,071 --> 00:39:00,075
I'm powerless.
It's a disease.

665
00:39:12,838 --> 00:39:14,131
Checkmate.

666
00:39:15,632 --> 00:39:18,802
Hey Jane.
I got Manchester to sign the warrant.

667
00:39:18,927 --> 00:39:19,970
I'm going to meet Van Pelt.

668
00:39:20,763 --> 00:39:23,265
Excellent police work
prevails yet again.

669
00:39:24,850 --> 00:39:26,060
Grieving parents at 12:00.

670
00:39:28,228 --> 00:39:31,357
- Mr. Jane, thank you.
- Thank you, sir.

671
00:39:32,608 --> 00:39:34,943
Much appreciated.
It's my pleas...

672
00:39:35,069 --> 00:39:38,155
Alth... I... was just heading...
I'll leave you to it.

673
00:39:39,740 --> 00:39:41,200
I have something for you.

674
00:39:43,327 --> 00:39:44,370
Your necklace.

675
00:39:44,870 --> 00:39:46,538
Charlie was trying
to get it back for you.

676
00:39:47,206 --> 00:39:48,248
Thank you.

677
00:39:49,458 --> 00:39:51,460
I want you to know that
your daughter changed.

678
00:39:52,294 --> 00:39:54,880
She knew that she hurt you both
and she wanted to make it right.

679
00:39:56,215 --> 00:39:57,257
She loved you.

680
00:40:00,135 --> 00:40:01,178
Our baby.

681
00:40:03,138 --> 00:40:04,181
Our poor baby.

682
00:40:12,189 --> 00:40:13,232
Lisbon.

683
00:40:14,233 --> 00:40:16,860
Hello, Teresa.
How are you today?

684
00:40:17,945 --> 00:40:21,198
- Fantastic, actually.
- Oh, I can imagine.

685
00:40:22,825 --> 00:40:24,201
The thrill of the chase
and all that.

686
00:40:26,036 --> 00:40:28,705
I'm not sure I know what
you're referring to, Mr. Volker.

687
00:40:29,456 --> 00:40:30,624
"Oh, don't be modest."

688
00:40:32,000 --> 00:40:36,255
I'm calling to congratulate you.
The warrant for Charles Milk.

689
00:40:39,091 --> 00:40:41,927
- How did you know about that?
- "Oh, I have my ways."

690
00:40:43,053 --> 00:40:46,098
At any rate, you won't find
what you're looking for.

691
00:40:47,766 --> 00:40:51,103
Charles Milk did a few personal
security jobs for me, nothing more.

692
00:40:51,979 --> 00:40:55,441
But, hey, he's a great guy.
I'm sure you'll enjoy him.

693
00:40:56,108 --> 00:41:01,196
- If that's it, I've got another call.
- By all means, you should take that.

694
00:41:04,658 --> 00:41:07,661
- Van Pelt, I'm on my way.
- We're too late.

695
00:41:20,757 --> 00:41:21,800
We've just I.D.'d them all.

696
00:41:24,887 --> 00:41:26,930
We've got a married couple,
Bob and Sylvia Miller

697
00:41:27,639 --> 00:41:29,099
and this gentleman
is Charles Milk.

698
00:41:30,100 --> 00:41:31,143
What happened here?

699
00:41:31,643 --> 00:41:33,812
Drive-by shooting.
Some gang b.s.

700
00:41:34,438 --> 00:41:36,523
These three were just
in the wrong place at the wrong time.

